            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="4" spacingafter="0" leftindent="8.65 in" rightindent="0.25 in">C001 generates upward line loads from prescribed pressures and the live deck width. C004 applies the windward-quarter-point eccentricity with concurrent horizontal wind to determine bearing reactions and stability.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="4" spacingafter="0" leftindent="8.65 in" rightindent="0.25 in">Variables: p_V_III; w_V_III; e_V; w_U_III; m_U_III; m_OT_III</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="10" spacingafter="0" leftindent="8.65 in" rightindent="0.25 in" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#154E79" texthighlight="#EAF1F7">SCOPE / REVIEW NOTE</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="4" spacingafter="0" leftindent="8.65 in" rightindent="0.25 in">The source article includes Strength III and Service IV vertical wind. Only Strength III is used in the current pier load sets. Moments and bearing reactions are derived equilibrium results; C002 does not perform the uplift check.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingbefore="4" spacingafter="0" leftindent="8.65 in" rightindent="0.25 in">
                <link address="#CodeReferencesGeneral.CodePage10;paragraphprojectcoderef10General">Related: LRFD 3.8.1.2.3a-b; Table 3.8.1.2.3a-1</link>
